<title>PERU: Peru's January coffee output falls to 15 tonnes.</title>
<headline>Peru's January coffee output falls to 15 tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's January coffee production fell to 15 tonnes from 62 tonnes in the same month last year, the Agriculture Ministry said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Non-decaffeinated coffee exports fell 68.6 percent in December to $5.1 million, while total exports last year fell 21.5 percent from 1995 to $222.6 million, the ministry added in its monthly report.</p>
<p>The ministry did not give export figures for January.</p>
<p>Peru, whose principal coffee harvest is between April and November, is South America's number four producer after Brazil, Colombia and Ecuador, according to the government.</p>
<p>((-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
